Original code, 2026, Apache-2.0, except the explicitly attributed MIT adaptations
crypto/src/main/java/xyz/kd5ujc/scarab/crypto/vrf/Ed25519Point.java and Draft03Math.java. Their source
notices and fixtures/vrf/licenses/CCL-LICENSE are retained unchanged.

fixtures/reference/spending-datum contains generated throwaway private-network transactions
and original reference-node verdicts, produced by this project's Apache-2.0 tooling. Only public
verification keys and signatures are retained; no signing keys are distributed.
Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses.

fixtures/fuzz/early-era-transactions contains synthetic Shelley, Allegra and Mary decoder seeds
serialized by the Apache-2.0 reference CLI 11.2.3.0 bundled in node release 11.1.3. The input is
synthetic and witness sets are empty; no signing keys or ledger-admission claim are included.
The generated inputs are distributed under this project's Apache-2.0 license.

fixtures/reference/plutus-data-chunks contains synthetic CBOR inputs and original parser/hash
verdicts from the same reference CLI, under the project's Apache-2.0 license. No node was contacted.

This source distribution includes test fixtures derived from Cardano Ledger,
Cardano Base, Ouroboros Network, Ouroboros Consensus, Amaru and Scalus-node.
Original upstream licenses and notices are retained under fixtures/licenses and
the per-fixture directories named below. No upstream implementation source is
vendored beyond the retained fixture/evidence excerpts.

Byron version fixtures (fixtures/byron-version): synthetic signed proposal generated by the
Apache-2.0 reference CLI 11.2.3.0 bundled in node release 11.1.3, plus byte-mutated
protocol-version fields and recorded raw decoder verdicts. Only the throwaway key's public
verification key and signature are retained; no signing key is included. Upstream notices
for the reference ledger are retained in fixtures/licenses.

Network fixtures (fixtures/network): manually specified and source-derived
handshake, mux, BlockFetch and KeepAlive envelopes from Ouroboros Network
(KeepAlive pin: commit c45735a56c567fa977969173d18943bac6bb3821) and Scalus-node,
plus Ouroboros Consensus-derived payloads, all Apache-2.0. Licenses and NOTICE
files are retained in fixtures/licenses, and the KeepAlive license beside
fixtures/network/keepalive-direct-range/manifest.json. Source-derived envelopes
are not captured upstream runtime transcripts. The Scala implementation is
independent.

VRF (fixtures/vrf): the draft03 verifier adapts Bloxbean CCL Ed25519Point.java
and VrfUtil.java at commit 45906b783973b4c44ac6883253af26bdd07bc1b4 under MIT.
The full CCL copyright/permission notice is retained in
fixtures/vrf/licenses/CCL-LICENSE. Cardano sodium source-derived public
fixtures retain the ISC notice in fixtures/vrf/licenses/sodium-LICENSE.
Bouncy Castle's notice is retained alongside it. No native binary, prover,
signer or keygen is bundled.

Ed25519 witnesses (fixtures/witness): public-only sodium, speccheck, Wycheproof
and ledger fixture projections with their ISC, Apache-2.0 and MIT/CC0/BSD
attribution files in fixtures/witness/licenses. The curve25519-elisabeth 0.1.3
arithmetic artifact is a runtime dependency (see "Third-party runtime dependencies"); no
signing implementation or private-key corpus is vendored.

Leios (fixtures/leios): serialisation test vectors from IntersectMBO/cardano-base
(Apache-2.0; fixtures/licenses/cardano-base-LICENSE and -NOTICE), the golden LeiosVote of
IntersectMBO/ouroboros-consensus branch leios-prototype (Apache-2.0), and the throwaway
proto-devnet BLS test keys and genesis proofs of input-output-hk/ouroboros-leios (Apache-2.0).
Provenance per file is in fixtures/leios/README.md. The recorded testnet handshake replies are
protocol bytes.

Operational certificates (fixtures/opcert): the exact ledger OCert source and
four public Amaru header fixtures with their Apache-2.0 LICENSE/NOTICE files
under fixtures/opcert/evidence. The Scala adapter is original public-only code.

Sum6 KES (fixtures/sum6) and Praos headers (fixtures/praos): source-derived from
IntersectMBO/cardano-base revision 060819b59c184b951a54e3c563304983c53a3eac,
Apache-2.0, with public Amaru header fixtures under the Amaru license. Retained
sources and exact-target LICENSE files are under the respective evidence
directories; original notices remain in those files. Immutable pins are in
fixtures/sum6/evidence/sources.json.

The Conway ledger-derived witness fixtures originate in the Haskell
cardano-ledger-conformance-tests, distributed through cardano-blueprint and
Amaru; their verbatim licenses are fixtures/licenses/cardano-ledger-conformance-LICENSE,
cardano-ledger-conformance-NOTICE, blueprint-conformance-LICENSE and amaru-LICENSE.

Captured chain data (fixtures/mainnet, fixtures/preview, fixtures/mempack): public blockchain data fetched from the
public Cardano relays (fixtures/mempack: 95 ledger outputs of the Mithril preprod snapshot); fixtures/preview also holds records derived from the Koios public API
(https://koios.rest). fixtures/eras, fixtures/haskell-state (ledger snapshots written by the reference
node 11.1.3 tooling) and fixtures/kes-gen are produced from a throwaway local cluster
and carry no third-party data. The files in fixtures/licenses and the licence files of the
individual fixture directories cover the upstream-derived test vectors.

The reference Cardano node binaries used by scripts/prepare_reference_image.py are
the official IntersectMBO 11.1.3 release (Apache-2.0); they are downloaded by the
user and never redistributed in this repository.

Plutus evaluation: the node depends at runtime on Scalus (org.scalus:scalus_3 1.4.0,
https://github.com/scalus3/scalus, Apache-2.0) for the UPLC machine and its builtins only; the
script context, cost-model selection and phase-2 rules are original code written against the
Cardano ledger's published behaviour. Scalus brings org.scalus:scalus-crypto-jni 0.1.0 (Apache-2.0),
whose jar bundles one native library per platform (Linux x86_64/arm64, macOS x86_64/arm64,
Windows x64), extracted at run time by org.scijava:native-lib-loader 2.5.0 (BSD-2-Clause). Each
library statically links libsodium (ISC; the IOG fork, commit dbb48cce), libsecp256k1 v0.3.2
(bitcoin-core, MIT) and blst v0.3.15 (supranational, Apache-2.0). Their licence texts, taken from
the pinned upstream sources because the jars carry none, are plutus/licenses/LICENSE-libsodium,
plutus/licenses/LICENSE-libsecp256k1, plutus/licenses/LICENSE-native-lib-loader and
blst-native/LICENSE-blst. The jars are retrieved from Maven Central at build time and never
redistributed in this repository. Scalus's own ledger-to-script-context translation is consulted
only as a test oracle.

