fixtures/reference/context-errors contains generated throwaway private-network signed transactions
and outputs of unchanged released Cardano Ledger context-collection/encoding APIs. Derived API inputs
are explicitly distinguished from ledger admission. Public keys/signatures only; no signing keys.
The thin oracle wrapper is original Apache-2.0 code; upstream package licenses/notices remain under
fixtures/licenses and in the fetched source distributions.

fixtures/reference/script-results contains one byte-identical original admission control from the
context-errors corpus and explicitly marked API-only multi-script derivations with unchanged released
Cardano Ledger evaluation/encoding outputs. Public keys/signatures only; no signing keys. The thin
oracle wrapper and fixture generation are original Apache-2.0 code; upstream notices remain as above.

storage/src/test/resources/rewards-1.19.0.1 contains deterministic synthetic state and outputs of
unchanged released Cardano Ledger reward APIs. No upstream implementation is copied into the thin
Apache-2.0 wrapper in scripts/oracle/rewards. Package provenance, scope and hashes are retained with
the fixtures; upstream package licenses and notices remain in fixtures/licenses and fetched sources.

fixtures/snapshot-v5 contains native snapshot encodings of the repository's throwaway era/Preview
state fixtures and a native-writer reproduction, with pinned source/conversion provenance in its
manifest and README. The conversion wrapper is original Apache-2.0 code. Public state, keys and
signatures only; no signing keys or operational node data.

The functional conformance corpora under node/src/test/resources/upstream/conway-governance-functional,
node/src/test/resources/upstream/conway-native-ledgers, network/src/test/resources/upstream/mux-lifecycle
and storage/src/test/resources/rewards-timing-1.19.0.1 retain deterministic generated inputs and
unchanged Haskell reference outcomes. Only public keys/signatures, synthetic state and protocol
payloads are included; no signing keys. Original upstream pins, Apache-2.0 source/observer provenance
and package notices are recorded in their READMEs/manifests and the existing fixture license files.

fixtures/reference/context-matrix contains original public throwaway transaction inputs from the
v1-context/context-errors corpora and explicitly marked API-only derivations, with unchanged
